msgstr "`git checkout [-f|--ours|--theirs|-m|--conflict=<style>] [<tree-ish>] --pathspec-from-file=<file> [--pathspec-file-nul]`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-checkout.adoc:90
msgid ""
"Replace the specified files and/or directories with the version from the "
"index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-checkout.adoc:94
msgid ""
"For example, if you check out a commit, edit `file.txt`, and then decide "
"those changes were a mistake, `git checkout file.txt` will discard any "
"unstaged changes to `file.txt`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-checkout.adoc:101
msgid ""
"This will fail if the file has a merge conflict and you haven't yet run `git "
"add file.txt` (or something equivalent) to mark it as resolved.  You can use "
"`-f` to ignore the unmerged files instead of failing, use `--ours` or `--"
"theirs` to replace them with the version from a specific side of the merge, "
"or use `-m` to replace them with the original conflicted merge result."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-checkout.adoc:102
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "'git checkout' (-p|--patch) [<tree-ish>] [--] [<pathspec>...]"
msgid "`git checkout (-p|--patch) [<tree-ish>] [--] [<pathspec>...]`"
msgstr "`git checkout (-p|--patch) [<tree-ish>] [--] [<pathspec>...]`"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-checkout.adoc:107
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "This is similar to the previous mode, but lets you use the interactive "
#| "interface to show the \"diff\" output and choose which hunks to use in "
#| "the result.  See below for the description of `--patch` option."
msgid ""
"This is similar to the previous two modes, but lets you use the interactive "
"interface to show the \"diff\" output and choose which hunks to use in the "
"result.  See below for the description of `--patch` option."
msgstr ""
"これは以前のモードと似ていますが、対話的インターフェイスを使用して「diff」出"
"力を表示し、その結果において使用するハンクを選択できます。 `--patch` オプショ"
"ンの説明については、以下を参照してください。"

